lang: preserve stable alternative worlds and reject ungrounded unions

Normal-rule reducts extend the contextual rule model with completed stable-world
checking, exhaustive finite alternatives, and distinct logical/unfinished reports.
Concrete edit sessions exercise the two-rule program, withdrawal/reassertion,
versioned reissue, and grounded cycles. No landed theorem gains a premise.

Decision: LANG-72. New modules only; decisions/lang.md append-only.
Validation: scoped Lang.Proofs.Contextual.Worlds build (6G, two threads,
default 200000 heartbeats), five real mutation plants and restored GREEN probes.
Independent disjunct reader required before ROOT lands; worker does not land.

